# Delete and revoke (roadmap l4.md L12; tests/programs/revoke.asm): a copy
# of a segment loaded in DS, its parent revoked, is null on the way back;
# untyped revoked gives its memory back, made again at the same base; an
# endpoint revoked and deleted fails the call queued on it with KE_CAP
# (1); a worker's space and thread, made of untyped of their own, go with
# it; and E3's ABA case: across a call to a worker whose space has another
# segment in the same slot, each reads its own. A worker that deletes its
# own stack is stopped after its way back has failed three times; copies of
# untyped and of a saved reply are refused with KE_ARG (2). The
# demonstration's kill gives a program's memory back too (tests/demo).
program: revoke
define: TEST_CAPS
---
rx286, test build
revoke: a copy in DS, its parent revoked: DS (0): 0
revoke: the untyped revoked, its segment still there (0): 0
revoke: memory given back, made again at the same base (1): 1
revoke: the worker's queued call, its endpoint deleted: status (1): 1
revoke: a worker's untyped revoked: its thread gone (1): 1
revoke: the worker read, in its own slot (66): 66
revoke: and the program, in its own, after the call (65): 65
rx286: program fault #GP(0014) at 0007:{worker.stranded_back}
rx286: program fault #GP(0014) at 0007:{worker}
rx286: program fault #GP(0014) at 0007:{worker}
rx286: a thread cannot go back to its ring: stopped
revoke: a worker without its stack: stopped (8): 8
revoke: untyped copied: status (2): 2
revoke: a saved reply copied: status (2): 2
revoke: done
